nvenience<\/span><\/strong><\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 26.4706%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #003a70;\">&nbsp;<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 7.02614%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #003a70;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>&nbsp;<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 28.7582%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #003a70;\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<\/tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 53.8375px;\">\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 37.7451%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">Ambient Lighting<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 26.4706%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">SEL Premium and Above<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 7.02614%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">-&gt;<\/span><br><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 28.7582%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p>Limited<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<\/tr>\r\n<\/tbody>\r\n<\/table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","excerptPreview":null,"contentPreview":"2027 Hyundai Kona (ICE) \u2013 Carry-over Model ITEM CHANGE FROM \u201826 MY CHANGE TO \u201827 MY Mechanical Idle Stop and Go (ISG) SE -> Dropped Interior \/ Convenience Ambient Lighting SEL Premium and Above -> Limited","sort":0,"published":"Jul 16, 2026"},{"id":248,"title":"2027 Hyundai Kona","excerpt":null,"content":"<p>The Hyundai Kona is the brand&rsquo;s entry crossover SUV, positioned below the Tucson in its SUV lineup. It is designed for buyers who want a smaller, more urban-friendly SUV with available gasoline and electric powertrains. Kona Electric is the battery-electric version of Kona and is part of Hyundai&rsquo;s EV lineup alongside IONIQ 5 and IONIQ 9.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Key facts<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>Vehicle type: Compact SUV<br>Powertrain: 2.0L MPI Atkinson Engine with Intelligent Variable transmission, and 1.6T-GDI Startstream engine with 8-Speed automatic transmission<br>Drive layout: Standard FWD; Optional HTRAC AWD (all trims)<br>Charging architecture: Four USB-C Charge ports 15W<br>Maximum output: 190 hp \/ 195 lb-ft (1.6T-GDI Smartstream engine)<br>Trims referenced: SE, SEL Sport, SEL Premium, Limited<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Powertrain overview<br><\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p>The 2027 Kona offers two gasoline powertrains: a 147-hp 2.0L Atkinson-cycle four-cylinder paired with an Intelligent Variable Transmission (IVT), and a more powerful 190-hp 1.6L turbocharged four-cylinder paired with an 8-speed automatic transmission. Both engines are available with standard front-wheel drive or optional HTRAC all-wheel drive, allowing buyers to choose between efficiency-focused and performance-oriented configurations.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Performance highlights<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>Maximum power: 190 HP @ 6000 rpm<br>Maximum torque: 195 lb-ft @ 1700-4500 rpm<br>Drivetrain: FWD standard; HTRAC, AWD available<br>Transmission: Intelligent Variable Transmission and 8-Speed Automatic<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Safety &amp; driver assistance<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>The 2027 Kona comes standard with Hyundai SmartSense safety technologies, including Forward Collision-Avoidance Assist with Pedestrian\/Cyclist Detection, Lane Keeping Assist, Lane Following Assist, Blind-Spot Collision Warning, Rear Cross-Traffic Collision-Avoidance Assist, and Smart Cruise Control with Stop &amp; Go. New safety enhancements include Junction Turning and Direct Oncoming collision avoidance, haptic steering wheel alerts, and upgraded second-row seatbelt systems. The Limited trim adds advanced features such as Surround View Monitor, Blind-Spot View Monitor, Parking Distance Warning, Parking Collision-Avoidance Assist-Reverse, and Remote Smart Parking Assist.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Dimensions &amp; utility<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>Wheelbase: 104.7 in<br>Overall length: 171.3 in <br>Overall width: 71.9 in<br>Overall height: FWD: 17\/18-inch wheels: 62.2 (62.4), 19-inch wheels: 62.4 (62.6) AWD: 17\/18-inch wheels: 63.2 (63.4), 19-inch wheels: 63.4 (63.6<br>Cargo volume: 25.5 cu. ft<br>Coefficient of drag: 0.302<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Trim overview<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>The 2027 Kona lineup ranges from the entry-level SE and sporty SEL Sport to the more upscale SEL Premium, while the Limited serves as the fully loaded flagship with premium comfort, technology, and safety features.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Awards<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p><strong>Award: 2026 Best Adventure Vehicles&nbsp;<br><\/strong>Category: Best Subcompact SUV<br>Year: 2026<br>Issued by: US News &amp; World Report<br>Applicable to: 2026 Kona<br>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/cars.usnews.com\/cars-trucks\/advice\/best-adventure-vehicles\">U.S. News &amp; World Report<\/a><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Award: IIHS 2026 Top Safety Award<br><\/strong>Category: TSP+ Winners<br>Year: 2026<br>Issued by: Insurance Institute for Highway Safety<br>Applicable to: 2026 Kona<br>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.iihs.org\/\">Insurance Institute of Highway Safety<\/a><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Award: 2026 Best Buy<br><\/strong>Category: Best Subcompact SUV<br>Year: 2026<br>Issued by: Kelley Blue Book<br>Applicable to: 2026 Kona<br>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.kbb.com\/awards\/best-buy-awards-2026\/\">Kelley Blue Book<\/a><\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Specification PDF download &amp; source<\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.hyundainews.com\/assets\/applications\/original\/72133-2027-kona-specs-features-20260715.pdf\">Download the 2027 Hyundai Kona Specifications and Features PDF<\/a><\/p>","excerptPreview":null,"contentPreview":"The Hyundai Kona is the brand\u2019s entry crossover SUV, positioned below the Tucson in its SUV lineup. It is designed for buyers who want a smaller, more urban-friendly SUV with available gasoline and electric powertrains. Kona Electric is the battery-electric version of Kona and is part of Hyundai\u2019s EV lineup alongside IONIQ 5 and IONIQ 9. Key facts Vehicle type: Compact SUVPowertrain:...","sort":0,"published":"Sep 8, 2026"}],"documents":[],"siblingsAndSelf":[],"images_count":0,"videos_count":0,"documents_count":0}],"releases":[],"images":[{"id":71785,"title":"2027 Kona","description":null,"created":"2026-07-10 15:50:49","type":"Image","folder":"\/production\/cf_view\/assets\/images\/original\/","name":"71785-66926-large624212025kona.jpg","private":1,"media_type":"image","options":{"mime":"image\/jpeg","wh":"6192 x 4128","size":"4.82 mb","extensions":["jpg","jpeg","jpe","jfif"],"img_sizes":["thumbnail","thumbnail-true","thumbnail-email","medium","small"]},"url":"\/assets\/images\/original\/71785-66926-large624212025kona.jpg","s3_url":"\/assets\/images\/{{variant}}\/71785-66926-large624212025kona.jpg","shared_url":null,"gif_url":null,"published":"Jul 16, 2026"},{"id":71784,"title":"2027 Kona","description":null,"created":"2026-07-10 15:50:47","type":"Image","folder":"\/production\/cf_view\/assets\/images\/original\/","name":"71784-66925-large624202025kona.jpg","private":1,"media_type":"image","options":{"mime":"image\/jpeg","wh":"6104 x 4069","size":"3.43 mb","extensions":["jpg","jpeg","jpe","jfif"],"img_sizes":["thumbnail","thumbnail-true","thumbnail-email","medium","small"]},"url":"\/assets\/images\/original\/71784-66925-large624202025kona.jpg","s3_url":"\/assets\/images\/{{variant}}\/71784-66925-large624202025kona.jpg","shared_url":null,"gif_url":null,"published":"Jul 16, 2026"},{"id":71802,"title":